data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1646996054224" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="1" data-id="1646996054224"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h1 class="vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-heading-2">I Watched My Son Pick A Screen Over Everything Else... Until One Book Quietly Pulled Him Back</h1></div></div><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1646996054132" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1646996054132" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center vy-vy-vy-gf_elm-left-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-lg" data-exc=""><img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-342-prime-naturals/images/img-7b.jpg" alt="" class="vy-vy-vy-gf_image vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyloaded vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload_done" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="2075" height="1020" natural-width="2075" natural-height="1020" data-lg-size="3000x3000" data-lazy-loaded="1500"></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1666271568587" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1666271568587"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p>The first thing that ever went up against the tablet and actually won</p></div></div><div data-label="Row" data-key="row" data-atomgroup="row" id="r-1666256039955" class="vy-vy-vy-gf_row vy-vy-vy-gf_row-gap-0" data-icon="gpicon-row" data-id="1666256039955" data-layout-lg="3+9" data-extraclass="" data-layout-md="3+9" data-layout-sm="3+9" data-layout-xs="3+9" data-row-gap="0px" style="display: block; flex-wrap: unset; visibility: visible;"><div class="vy-vy-vy-gf_column vy-vy-vy-gf_col-lg-3 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-md-3 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-sm-3 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-xs-3" id="c-1666256039933" data-id="1666256039933" style="display: block; flex-direction: unset; justify-content: unset; min-height: auto;"><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1666256087394" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1666256087394" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center vy-vy-vy-gf_elm-left-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs" data-exc=""><img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-342-prime-naturals/images/img-8.png" alt="" class="vy-vy-vy-gf_image vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyloaded vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload_done" data-gemlang="en" width="1024" height="1024" data-width="70px" data-height="auto" title="" natural-width="1024" natural-height="1024" data-lg-size="3000x3000" data-lazy-loaded="120"></div></div></div><div class="vy-vy-vy-gf_column vy-vy-vy-gf_col-lg-9 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-md-9 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-sm-9 vy-vy-vy-gf_col-xs-9" id="c-1666256043251" data-id="1666256043251" style="display: block; flex-direction: unset; justify-content: unset; min-height: auto;"><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1666256157280" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1666256157280"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p><b>5 Min Read · Written By Laura Bennett</b></p></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1666256182914" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1666256182914"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p><i>Laura is a mom of two who spent years losing the same fight over screens, from tablets at the dinner table to the meltdowns every time the iPad came away.</i></p></div></div></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1646996054153" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1646996054153"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p>I take dinner together seriously. Phones down, real talk, the kind of evening I grew up with.</p><p><br></p><p>Every few weeks I told myself this was when I would finally get my son off the tablet for good. Then the days went by, he was right back on it, and I felt like I was talking to the top of his head.</p><p><br></p><p>It was the same fight on repeat.</p><p><br></p><p>The nagging went nowhere. The screen always won. And I could not find one single thing that held his attention the way YouTube did.</p><p><br></p><p>I still remember a birthday dinner at my mom's house where he sat with his head down and a game going the whole time, like the rest of us were not even in the room.</p></div></div><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1646996054239" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1646996054239" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center vy-vy-vy-gf_elm-left-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-sm vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-center-lg" data-exc=""><img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-342-prime-naturals/images/img-9.jpg" alt="" class="vy-vy-vy-gf_image vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyloaded vy-vy-vy-gf_lazyload_done" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1520" height="800" natural-width="1520" natural-height="800" data-lg-size="3000x3000" data-lazy-loaded="1500"></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1646996054183" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1646996054183"><div class="vy-vy-vy-elm vy-vy-vy-text-edit vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-xs vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-md vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-sm vy-vy-vy-gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 vy-vy-vy-gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p><font face="Open Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif">Sound familiar?</font></p><p><br></p><p><font face="Open Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif">So I kept buying things I thought would help. New toys, board games, an art kit, all of it gathering dust the second he had a screen within reach.</font></p><p><br></p><p><font face="Open Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif">Months of trying, and I still could not name one thing that held him longer than the two minutes it took to get bored and ask for the tablet.</font></p><p><br></p><p><font face="Open Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif">And it was not only at home. The same thing happened in the car, at the doctor's office, waiting for food at a restaurant, anywhere there was a spare minute the screen came right back out.</font></p><p><br></p><p><font face="Open Sans, Helvetica, sans-serif">It got to the point where I just handed over the tablet to keep the peace, then sat there feeling guilty about it for the rest of the night.</font></p></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1666252116681" class="vy-vy-vy-element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="1" da